    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. (The lone `ERROR ExceptionControllerAdvice` line is expected output from a negative test case, not a failure.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Changes to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n\n1. **Monotonic sequence** \u2014 added a process-wide `static final AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ`, shared across all controller instances so `seq` strictly increases across every create for the life of the process.\n\n2. **Event emission** \u2014 right after the existing human-readable audit line, `addOwner` now also calls `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(...)`, which logs via the same `AUDIT` logger an immutable JSON object:\n   ```json\n   {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n   ```\n   Built as an SLF4J-parameterized message (the empty `{}` slots are placeholders; the literal JSON braces are not), so it's a single immutable formatted line.\n\n3. **Future-proofing the identifier** \u2014 I extracted a `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns the owner's current primary identifier. Today it returns `customerCode`; per the spec, when the customer code is later unified into the member id, that one method is the single place to switch to `memberId`, and the event automatically carries the new identifier in the same slot \u2014 exactly the migration the checkpoint description anticipates.\n\nThe new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes, confirming one AUDIT line contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode together; the full suite (264 tests) remains green.",
